  "comments": "<p>In 2004, the Surinamese gulden was replaced by the Surinamese dollar. This coin was revalued at 1/10 of a dollar.<br>&nbsp;</p><p>The Standard Catalog of World Coins originally stated that coins from 1987 to 1989 were made of nickel plated steel and classified them as KM# 13a. This has been corrected and those years are now classified as KM# 13. The current definition of KM# 13a is for nickel plated steel coins produced in 2021.<br><br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/64d949f2f0497.png\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/64d949f2f0497.png\" alt=\"\"></a><br>Coat of arms of Suriname (Source: Wikipedia)</p>",
